// The cockpit world's registry — every object you can fly to.
//
// ADDING SOMETHING TO THE UNIVERSE = ADDING ONE ENTRY HERE. Nothing else in the
// world engine knows object names or positions. (David, 2026-10-04: "a large open
// space so we can add more into the game and not need a redesign".)
//
// Coordinates are world units; the playable space is ±WORLD_HALF on both axes and
// the ship spawns near (0, 0) beside the Mirror. West = the home system (the main
// 37 game). East = the Far Side (Sector 73's own modes).
//
// `launch` says what LAUNCH on the docking card does:
//   { type: 'sector', mode, params? } → a Sector 73 mode, opened over the world (params: what it opens with)
//   { type: 'route', to, state }    → a real app route (the main game's screens)
//   { type: 'return' }              → back to the 37 home screen
// `paint` drives the procedural painter (world/painter.js) until real art exists;
// set `sprite: '<url>'` to draw an image instead.
// `icon` (+ optional `arrowColor`) gives the object an edge arrow while it is off-screen
// (world/edgeArrows.js, W5 2026-10-19): the four games and the Star Market have one.

// Grown 1.5x on 2026-10-14 (David: room for up to 37 pilots per server): objects are placed in the
// original layout below and spread out by SPREAD from the centre; their sizes stay the same.
export const WORLD_HALF = 5600; // 2026-10-14: bigger ships, so a roomier universe (was 4500)
export const SPREAD = 1.8; // was 1.45

// Daily + Practice (world lane, 2026-10-22, David): every game has a big DAILY object (`daily` = what
// it plays today: a Sector 73 game id, or 37's Daily mode) with a gold ring on the map, and a small
// grey PRACTICE moon beside it (`practiceOf` = its Daily object's id). A game's practice moon shows
// only once that game reads `params.entry` (./entryReady.js). One edge arrow per game's Daily:
// objects sharing an `arrowGroup` (37's three planets) get ONE arrow, to the nearest of them.

/** @typedef {{ type: 'sector', mode: string, params?: Record<string, any> } | { type: 'route', to: string, state?: object } | { type: 'return' }} Launch */
/** @typedef {{ id: string, name: string, kind: string, x: number, y: number, r: number, paint: object, launch: Launch, blurb: string, region: string, sprite?: string, tag?: string, tagColor?: string, icon?: string, arrowColor?: string, arrowGroup?: string, daily?: string, practiceOf?: string }} WorldObject */

